{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Go, serve</b>, etc. He spoke without specification and was cunning to keep it far [from thought] that it would not enter the mind that they would ask for all of them to go. Therefore he spoke without specification: ״לְכוּ עִבְדוּ״ (״Go, serve״), and he said <b>who and who</b> — not to say whether all of them, whether some of them; surely only the men of the service would go, as he revealed in the end: ״לְכוּ הַגְּבָרִים כִּי אוֹתָהּ אַתֶּם מְבַקְשִׁים״ (״Go, the men, for that is what you are seeking״). But even regarding the men, he did not want all of them to go."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:17.595716154Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}